; Tutorial_6_Select_and_Copy_a_Passage.inix -- selecting and gathering text.

[about]
Title=6 - Select and Copy a Passage
Intro=A passage selected in two keys rather than a drag, copied, the line copied when nothing is selected, passages gathered with Copy Append, and the whole page copied without its furniture.
Setup=HomerView is open on a long page.
Homework=Gather three passages from one page into one note with Alt plus C, and paste it into a document.

[step]

Say=One want: three passages from different parts of a page in one note, without a second window to paste into.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus Shift plus H opens the HomerView browser, or brings it back.
Key=Alt+Control+Shift+H
Hear=HomerView
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I move to where the passage begins. F8 starts the selection.
Key=F8
Hear=Start Selection
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I move to where it ends, by arrow, by heading or by find. Shift plus F8 completes it.
Key=Shift+F8
Hear=(the selected passage)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus C copies it. With nothing selected, Control plus C copies the line I am on, which the browser's own copy does not.
Key=Control+C
Hear=Copied
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=For the second passage, Alt plus C, Copy Append, adds it to what is already on the clipboard, with a blank line between.
Key=Alt+C
Hear=Appended
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: Control plus C for the third passage would replace the first two. Alt plus C again keeps all three.
Key=Alt+C
Hear=Appended
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus F8 copies the whole page, without its navigation and footers.
Key=Control+F8
Hear=(the page, copied)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the command; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Start, then complete a selection.
Key=
Hear=F8
Hear=Shift plus F8

[step]

Say=Control plus Space selects the chunk at the cursor, a run of characters with no spaces in it, such as a web address or a code.
Key=Control+Space
Hear=selected
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus Space says what is selected, or spells it if pressed twice.
Key=Shift+Space
Hear=ABC-1234
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus F8 returns to where the selection began, to check its start.
Key=Alt+Shift+F8
Hear=Start of selection
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Apostrophe saves the clipboard to a text file, proposing a name, so a passage gathered over several pages can be kept.
Key=Control+Apostrophe
Hear=Save Clipboard dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape. Control plus Shift plus Apostrophe adds the clipboard to the end of a text file, rather than replacing it.
Key=Escape
Hear=HomerView
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus Apostrophe empties the clipboard, so an append starts afresh.
Key=Alt+Shift+Apostrophe
Hear=Clipboard cleared
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus F8 reads the whole page aloud without moving the cursor, to hear a passage in context before copying it.
Key=

[step]

Say=These are the keys EdSharp uses for the same work, so a passage moves from a page to a document with the same habits.
Key=

[step]

Say=Copy Line, Control plus C, copies the selection, or the current line when nothing is selected, so one line needs no selecting at all.
Key=Control+C
Hear=Copied
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus C adds the selection, or the current line, to what is already on the clipboard, gathering lines from different places into one.
Key=Alt+C
Hear=Appended
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus F8 copies the whole page's text in one press, for pasting into a document of your own.
Key=Control+F8
Hear=All text copied
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Add to the clipboard.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus C
